This crate (`symphonia-codec-nellymoser`) is a from-scratch, pure-Rust Nellymoser Asao decoder. It is
licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

Nellymoser has no public specification. The bit allocation algorithm, the dequantization,
band-size, initial-value and delta tables (`src/tables.rs`, extracted programmatically), the
noise-substitution generator (FFmpeg's additive lagged Fibonacci generator `av_lfg`, seed 0), and
the block layout follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/nellymoser.c`, `libavcodec/nellymoserdec.c` and
`libavutil/lfg.c`, which are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or
later. FFmpeg's Nellymoser code is in turn derived from the nelly2pcm project
(http://code.google.com/p/nelly2pcm/).

